# ADR-0010: Safe Interface Construction on a Hardened Reference

## Status
**APPROVED — VALIDATION PHASE**  
*Not expansion — proof that guards enable value without drift*

## Goal
Prove that the hardened reference (Phase 3) can safely support real user interfaces **without breaking architectural boundaries**.  
This is validation of Phase 3 — not feature development.

## Unbreakable Rules (Violations block merge)
1. **Composition Root Enforcement**  
   All Use Cases MUST be instantiated ONLY via `src/shared/di_container.py`  
   → Direct instantiation outside di_container = merge blocked

2. **DTO Boundary Integrity**  
   Presentation layer MUST consume ONLY DTOs (never Domain Entities)  
   → `from src.domain.entities import *` in `src/presentation/` = merge blocked

3. **MessageMap Monopoly**  
   All user-facing text MUST flow through `src/presentation/messages/message_map.py`  
   → Hardcoded Arabic/English text outside MessageMap = merge blocked

4. **Zero Business Logic in Presentation**  
   `src/presentation/` MUST contain ONLY:  
   - Data formatting (DTO → CSV/PDF/HTML)  
   - Wiring (Composition Root invocation)  
   → Decision logic in presentation = merge blocked

## Why This Is Validation (Not Expansion)
| Phase 3 | Phase 4 |
|---------|---------|
| Proved boundaries CAN be locked | Proves locked boundaries DON'T prevent value |
| Guard scripts passing | Guard scripts passing WHILE delivering real CLI/reporting |
| Theoretical purity | Practical purity under pressure |

## Success Criteria
✅ Real user can complete workflow via CLI without touching code  
✅ All outputs stable under Snapshot Testing  
✅ Zero guard violations during entire Phase 4 execution  
✅ Legacy integration remains isolated in `tools/legacy/`  

## Signatures
Architecture Team — 2026-02-05  
*"The reference is not proven until it survives real usage."*